---
import CodeBlock from '../../../components/CodeBlock.astro'
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro'
import { recordExample, renderExample, streamExample } from '../../../lib/api-reference.js'
---

<DocsLayout
  title="API and CLI"
  description="Native browser, recording, media and publishing APIs."
  section="api"
>
  <h1>Native API and CLI</h1>
  <h2 id="public-exports">Public exports</h2>
  <p>
    <code>suitecut</code> exposes <code>record</code>, <code>defineSuiteCut</code>, <code
      >launchBrowser</code
    >, <code>createBroadcast</code>, <code>createNativePage</code> and <code>renderSuiteCut</code>.
    Lower-level source and recorder APIs live in <code>suitecut/native</code>. Audio plugins,
    rendering and manifest types have separate subpaths.
  </p>
  <h2 id="recording-options">Recording options</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={recordExample} />
  <p>
    Root recording owns its primary source. <code>recordNative</code> records a caller-owned source. Callback
    context contains the source, page, presentation fixture, cancellation signal and <code
      >addSource</code
    >.
  </p>
  <h2 id="fixture-methods">Fixture methods</h2>
  <p>
    Use <code>selectPage</code>, <code>narrate</code>, <code>checkpoint</code>, <code>hold</code>, <code
      >highlight</code
    >, <code>zoom</code>, <code>hover</code>, <code>click</code>, <code>type</code>, <code
      >scrollTo</code
    > and <code>scrollTop</code>. Checkpoints are video clips.
  </p>
  <h2 id="capture-options">Capture options</h2>
  <p>
    Native launch sets CSS dimensions, device scale 1 or 2, capture FPS 1–120 and BGRA/I420 format.
    Physical frames are bounded to 3840×2160. Recording capture sets output size/FPS, narration tail
    and boolean page audio.
  </p>
  <p>
    Strict CSS locators operate in the main document. Evaluation requires JSON-serializable values.
    Frame APIs, role/text locators, remote handles and popup/download workflows are not implemented.
  </p>
  <h2 id="render-api">Renderer</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={renderExample} />
  <h2 id="audio-plugin-api">Audio plugins</h2>
  <p>
    Configure local model providers with <code>audioPlugins</code>. The worker invokes <code
      >synthesize</code
    > and expects mono PCM WAV at the supplied output path.
  </p>
  <h2 id="action-zoom">Action zoom</h2>
  <p>
    Authored zoom is applied by the final renderer. Browser-rendered effects can appear in
    simultaneous broadcasts, but offline zoom and narration mixing do not affect them.
  </p>
  <h2 id="stream-options">Streaming API</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={streamExample} />
  <h2 id="word-timings">Word timings</h2>
  <p>
    Providers may return word timing artifacts for caption highlighting. Timing values are validated
    against the narration text and clip duration.
  </p>
  <h2 id="command-line-flags">CLI flags</h2>
  <CodeBlock
    label="Terminal"
    code={'node dist/cli.js install\nnode dist/cli.js doctor\nnode dist/cli.js render --manifest .suitecut/tour.json --output .suitecut/tour.mp4 --fps 60\nnode dist/cli.js --help'}
  />
  <h2 id="recorded-test">Verification</h2>
  <p>
    Run native unit tests and decoded cadence verification. Real browser verifiers additionally
    require the built CEF executable.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
